1
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:39,439
I met a little boy in the mountains.

2
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:42,480
Who could barely speak Mandarin.

3
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:43,959
An ethnic minority boy.

4
00:01:44,519 --> 00:01:45,680
He didn't seem to have much schooling, either.

5
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:46,680
How tall was he?

6
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:49,519
How tall was the little boy?

7
00:01:51,879 --> 00:01:54,480
About... this tall.

8
00:01:54,879 --> 00:01:56,439
So he saw you.

9
00:02:01,239 --> 00:02:02,040
And then?

10
00:02:02,319 --> 00:02:03,439
He lived in the woods

11
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,040
with his dad.

12
00:02:05,519 --> 00:02:06,560
His adoptive father, that is.

13
00:02:06,959 --> 00:02:08,840
The little boy was really cute.

14
00:02:09,599 --> 00:02:10,800
With dark skin.

15
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,000
And dark eyes.

16
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:13,680
And he gave every tree

17
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:15,000
a name that only he knew.

18
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:16,919
Every tree?

19
00:02:17,199 --> 00:02:18,800
Every tree had a name?

20
00:02:20,439 --> 00:02:22,759
As if the trees were his friends.

21
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:27,319
You... You just mentioned his adoptive father.

22
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:29,599
Right. That call just now

23
00:02:29,599 --> 00:02:31,960
was to tell me his adoptive father got arrested.

24
00:02:32,039 --> 00:02:35,759
And it seems the kid's family

25
00:02:35,759 --> 00:02:37,599
wants the child back.

26
00:02:37,599 --> 00:02:40,719
So the two sides got into some sort of conflict.

27
00:02:42,199 --> 00:02:43,280
People from Rongshan...

28
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:45,199
Why would they be arrested and brought here?

29
00:02:45,719 --> 00:02:47,479
They didn't explain it clearly on the phone.

30
00:02:47,479 --> 00:02:49,759
Anyway, they just want me to go over there.

31
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:52,400
Will you take Lao Kang's case?

32
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,000
I don't know.

33
00:02:57,479 --> 00:03:00,039
They probably just see me as a familiar face,

34
00:03:00,039 --> 00:03:02,240
and want me to help ask around about the situation.

35
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:04,400
Do you know if there are

36
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,800
any cheap and reliable budget hotels nearby?

37
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:09,319
How could a cheap one be reliable?

38
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,080
Why don't you choose a nicer, more comfortable one?

39
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:15,800
I'd love to.

40
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:16,479
But...

41
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:20,520
I'm in a bit of a tricky situation right now.

42
00:03:21,919 --> 00:03:22,599
Why?

43
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:28,759
To stop me from moving out, my mom

44
00:03:28,759 --> 00:03:30,400
cut off my financial support.

45
00:03:31,319 --> 00:03:32,240
So from now on, I can only

46
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,759
survive on the bonuses from my cases.

47
00:03:35,039 --> 00:03:37,639
But no one dares to bring me any cases now.

48
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:39,680
But I really can't

49
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:40,759
continue living like this.

50
00:03:40,759 --> 00:03:41,919
Then I'll lend you money.

51
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:43,439
Really?

52
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:45,360
No, I didn't ask you out

53
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:46,919
to borrow money from you.

54
00:03:46,919 --> 00:03:48,479
Have you considered that you're a girl?

55
00:03:48,479 --> 00:03:50,800
Why would you look for unsafe hotels?

56
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:54,080
You're also a lawyer, you know?

57
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:57,599
I'm not some hotshot lawyer with enemies.

58
00:03:57,599 --> 00:03:58,439
Listen to me.

59
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:01,240
It's because after you reported me,

60
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:03,639
you suffered a lot of negative backlash.

61
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,439
But I don't think you did anything wrong.

62
00:04:06,919 --> 00:04:09,120
If anything, you were dragged down with me.

63
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:10,000
Look,

64
00:04:11,879 --> 00:04:12,800
I appreciate the gesture.

65
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:14,759
But it's really unnecessary.

66
00:04:19,879 --> 00:04:20,800
Thank you.

67
00:04:21,759 --> 00:04:23,120
I can solve this myself.

68
00:04:27,399 --> 00:04:28,560
Alright, it's getting late.

69
00:04:29,079 --> 00:04:30,000
You should head back early.

70
00:04:35,279 --> 00:04:37,279
If you accept my proposal,

71
00:04:37,279 --> 00:04:39,439
we'll call it even for you reporting me.

72
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:43,639
Besides,

73
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:44,839
it's not a free loan.

74
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,040
You have to write an IOU.

75
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:46,920
Loans must be repaid,

76
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:48,199
and there will be interest.

77
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:54,120
Can't you let an unemployed old man

78
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:55,600
earn some extra cash?

79
00:05:11,079 --> 00:05:11,839
You'll need to write an IOU.

80
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:14,519
With interest, of course.

81
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,560
Okay.

82
00:05:17,759 --> 00:05:19,839
The people at your court gave me attitude,

83
00:05:19,839 --> 00:05:20,720
but I didn't regret it.

84
00:05:21,959 --> 00:05:24,040
My colleagues and boss talked behind my back,

85
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,079
but I still didn't regret it.

86
00:05:26,639 --> 00:05:28,519
Even when that male caregiver's girlfriend

87
00:05:28,519 --> 00:05:29,959
terminated her contract with me,

88
00:05:29,959 --> 00:05:30,879
I didn't regret it at all.

89
00:05:31,759 --> 00:05:33,360
But for a moment just now,

90
00:05:35,279 --> 00:05:37,000
I really kind of regretted reporting you.

91
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,279
Why? What do you mean?

92
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:43,439
I only mentioned

93
00:05:43,439 --> 00:05:45,120
the name Lao Kang once on the phone.

94
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:46,519
I can't believe you remembered.

95
00:05:49,639 --> 00:05:50,959
What do you think

96
00:05:50,959 --> 00:05:52,800
someone with Alzheimer's is like?

97
00:05:53,439 --> 00:05:54,480
Like a crashed computer?

98
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,920
Just a black screen with nothing on it?

99
00:05:57,199 --> 00:05:58,399
Let me tell you,

100
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:00,079
if you need a place to stay,

101
00:06:00,079 --> 00:06:02,800
you'd better go to 128 Zhongshan Road.

102
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:03,759
To that hotel.

103
00:06:04,759 --> 00:06:06,399
Because there's a police station next door.

104
00:06:06,639 --> 00:06:07,279
If anything happens,

105
00:06:07,279 --> 00:06:09,040
the police will be there in two minutes.

106
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:10,040
It's a bit safer.

107
00:06:12,279 --> 00:06:13,040
Will you remember?

108
00:06:13,279 --> 00:06:14,480
Write it down if you can't.

109
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:15,319
In case you forget.

110
00:06:20,519 --> 00:06:21,680
You decide how much to borrow.

111
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,000
I just transferred the money to you.

112
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:23,879
See if it's enough.

113
00:06:32,639 --> 00:06:34,000
Is it okay? Is it enough?

114
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:37,879
Thank you.

115
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:39,600
Thank me?

116
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:40,639
There will be interest.

117
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:44,240
Thank you for giving me a chance

118
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,279
to get even with you.

119
00:06:50,399 --> 00:06:52,879
First time borrowing money in my life.

120
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,480
What a coincidence.

121
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:57,240
It's my first time lending money to someone, too.

122
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:10,040
He gave every tree

123
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:11,480
a name only he knew,

124
00:07:13,639 --> 00:07:15,920
as if that tree were his friend.

125
00:07:36,399 --> 00:07:36,920
Hello?

126
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,279
Zhao Yijie, I want to ask you...

127
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:40,240
You said

128
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:44,879
you had already found a lawyer for Lao Kang.

129
00:07:45,399 --> 00:07:46,920
But today, a friend of mine

130
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:49,959
also got a call about Lao Kang's case.

131
00:07:49,959 --> 00:07:50,959
What does this mean?

132
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:52,480
This is none of your business.

133
00:07:58,319 --> 00:07:59,800
It just hasn't been driven in a while.

134
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:01,360
Change the tires and the battery,

135
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:02,759
then change the oil,

136
00:08:02,759 --> 00:08:04,160
and it should be fine.

137
00:08:04,399 --> 00:08:07,279
Lao Kong, I'm here on serious business.

138
00:08:07,519 --> 00:08:09,480
I need you to help me find someone's address.

139
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:10,560
That's easy.

140
00:08:11,439 --> 00:08:12,759
A few phone calls and I'll have it.

141
00:08:12,759 --> 00:08:13,360
Whose?

142
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:16,439
The founder of Rujie Law Firm, Zhao Yijie.

143
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,680
Name your price.

144
00:08:25,879 --> 00:08:27,000
I know the rules.

145
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,720
About what you just said,

146
00:08:28,959 --> 00:08:31,120
I couldn't do it for any amount of money.

147
00:08:31,279 --> 00:08:32,200
Why not?

148
00:08:33,879 --> 00:08:35,320
Can't you just help me this once?

149
00:08:35,879 --> 00:08:37,559
I am helping you right now.

150
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:42,039
Just stay out of this mess, okay?

151
00:08:43,399 --> 00:08:44,360
That place, Rujie...

152
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:46,000
I can't tell you too much about it.

153
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,120
Anyway, just trust me.

154
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:48,159
Stop asking around.

155
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:50,759
Lao Kong, you need to explain it to me today.

156
00:08:51,279 --> 00:08:52,000
Why?

157
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,519
You went to Rujie to look for Zhao Yijie.

158
00:08:55,519 --> 00:08:56,440
That's no secret.

159
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:58,039
Word has already spread.

160
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:00,000
Those law firms that wanted to hire you

161
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:00,919
have all given up.

162
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,159
Who in the entire legal circle isn't avoiding him?

163
00:09:03,159 --> 00:09:05,679
Whenever Zhao Yijie has his eye on someone or a case,

164
00:09:05,679 --> 00:09:07,320
no one dares to fight him for it.

165
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:09,360
That's my business.

166
00:09:10,799 --> 00:09:13,360
If I tell you where he lives,

167
00:09:15,159 --> 00:09:16,600
I have a wife and kids to think about.

168
00:09:17,399 --> 00:09:18,879
Lao Kong, I'm just curious.

169
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:22,039
You're not afraid to cause trouble at the court,

170
00:09:22,759 --> 00:09:23,679
but you're afraid of him?

171
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,080
What is he? The mafia?

172
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:28,440
The mafia is nothing compared to him.

173
00:09:28,919 --> 00:09:29,759
Let me tell you.

174
00:09:30,279 --> 00:09:31,519
Without Zhao Yijie,

175
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,679
half of Jiangliu City would stop running.

176
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,679
I've told you too much.

177
00:09:36,679 --> 00:09:38,600
I can't say anymore.

178
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:41,480
Alright then.

179
00:09:42,159 --> 00:09:43,440
I won't bother you anymore.

180
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:44,519
Thanks. I'll find someone else.

181
00:09:44,519 --> 00:09:45,120
No.

182
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:46,559
You can't ask anyone else.

183
00:09:46,559 --> 00:09:47,440
Whoever you ask,

184
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:49,600
word will get to Zhao Yijie's ears.

185
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:50,279
I get it.

186
00:09:50,279 --> 00:09:51,279
I'm unemployed now.

187
00:09:51,279 --> 00:09:52,399
People sure turn their backs fast, huh?

188
00:09:52,399 --> 00:09:53,679
That's uncalled for.

189
00:09:53,799 --> 00:09:54,960
You're so stubborn.

190
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:55,759
I give up.

191
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:58,879
Well, that receptionist at Rujie...

192
00:09:58,879 --> 00:10:00,000
She looks unremarkable,

193
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:03,120
but she actually helped Zhao Yijie build his business from scratch.

194
00:10:03,559 --> 00:10:04,720
If you want to know his address,

195
00:10:04,759 --> 00:10:05,879
follow that receptionist for a few days.

196
00:10:05,879 --> 00:10:06,919
You should get some results.

197
00:10:07,159 --> 00:10:08,080
Are you saying they...

198
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:10,559
Uh, I'll call you when the car is fixed.

199
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,919
I'll just drop it off at your house.

200
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:14,799
Go ahead and get busy.

201
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:21,519
I know, Mr. Ye.

202
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:22,879
Winning or losing a lawsuit

203
00:10:22,879 --> 00:10:24,559
is something no one can guarantee.

204
00:10:24,799 --> 00:10:26,200
If Lao Kang really broke the law,

205
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:27,159
then even the best lawyer

206
00:10:27,159 --> 00:10:29,399
couldn't argue that black is white for him.

207
00:10:31,679 --> 00:10:34,120
You mean the family that adopted Yang A'wu

208
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:35,399
got a lawyer for Lao Kang?

209
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:40,879
I'll call you back later.

210
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:42,080
Bye.

211
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:44,840
What did you want to see me about?

212
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:45,799
Good news.

213
00:10:46,679 --> 00:10:48,120
Rujie gave me a case.

214
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:50,000
An armed robbery from four years ago.

215
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:52,759
A criminal case?

216
00:10:53,159 --> 00:10:53,720
Yeah.

217
00:10:53,799 --> 00:10:54,960
And the client

218
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:57,399
is a distant relative of our boss.

219
00:10:58,080 --> 00:11:00,399
So if we handle this case well,

220
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,200
getting you into Rujie

221
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:04,759
shouldn't be a problem.

222
00:11:06,759 --> 00:11:08,320
I'm doing perfectly fine at Changyu.

223
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:09,639
Why would I go to Rujie?

224
00:11:11,039 --> 00:11:12,000
Is this all you wanted?

225
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,840
Out of all the lawyers I know,

226
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,600
you're the best at criminal cases.

227
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:21,120
So I was thinking,

228
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:22,320
maybe we could

229
00:11:22,759 --> 00:11:23,600
team up like the old days?

230
00:11:24,559 --> 00:11:26,240
A 60-40 split in your favor.

231
00:11:30,799 --> 00:11:31,559
Let me think about it.

232
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,679
What is there to hesitate about?

233
00:11:36,399 --> 00:11:39,320
This is a great stepping stone for you, Ding Ning.

234
00:11:39,759 --> 00:11:41,080
For a law firm like Rujie,

235
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,639
its industry reputation and status

236
00:11:42,639 --> 00:11:43,480
go without saying.

237
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,679
I know you don't care about that anyway.

238
00:11:44,679 --> 00:11:47,720
The point is, Rujie has top-tier clients.

239
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:50,120
You'll never have to worry about winning a case

240
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:52,320
only for the client to refuse to pay.

241
00:11:53,759 --> 00:11:54,840
Plus, at Rujie,

242
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:57,840
you only need to focus on one or two cases a year

243
00:11:57,840 --> 00:11:59,600
and that's enough to support yourself.

244
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:03,320
It's nothing like our mentor's low-margin, high-volume approach.

245
00:12:10,159 --> 00:12:11,279
I have to head out now.

246
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:13,879
Give me an answer tomorrow.

247
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:14,799
Okay?

248
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:23,279
I'm off.

249
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:47,000
Free to meet up in a bit?

250
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:51,919
The guy you mentioned before...

251
00:12:51,919 --> 00:12:53,960
The lunatic threatening to get back at me?

252
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,039
Did you find out who he is?

253
00:12:56,399 --> 00:12:57,080
I did.

254
00:12:57,559 --> 00:12:58,759
Just some bored guy.

255
00:12:58,759 --> 00:13:00,399
He's all talk.

256
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:01,919
Nothing to worry about.

257
00:13:01,919 --> 00:13:02,879
Crisis averted.

258
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:03,840
What about you?

259
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:07,039
Weren't you going to Rongshan?

260
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:08,960
Not anymore.

261
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:11,240
We couldn't agree on the price.

262
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,720
You know, as lawyers...

263
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:15,440
isn't it normal for us to charge?

264
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:16,000
Of course.

265
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,320
Why is it that whenever I bring up money,

266
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:18,480
it feels like I'm in the wrong?

267
00:13:19,639 --> 00:13:20,600
Having some sweet soup?

268
00:13:22,039 --> 00:13:22,879
Where did you buy it?

269
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,440
People line up for it every day.

270
00:13:25,519 --> 00:13:27,320
It's right by that mall over there.

271
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:29,240
I just joined the line.

272
00:13:29,399 --> 00:13:31,519
I waited in line all afternoon today.

273
00:13:32,159 --> 00:13:33,320
Try it and see if it's good.

274
00:13:40,799 --> 00:13:41,639
Give it here.

275
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,840
When I used to eat this stuff,

276
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:53,039
it was never this complicated.

277
00:13:53,799 --> 00:13:54,639
I'm really not used to it.

278
00:13:55,919 --> 00:13:58,879
Since you're not taking that case anymore,

279
00:13:59,679 --> 00:14:01,799
and with Lao Kang locked up,

280
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,639
what about the kid, Yang A'wu?

281
00:14:03,639 --> 00:14:04,559
How is he doing now?

282
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:06,000
Have you contacted him?

283
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:07,960
No.

284
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:11,759
But I've been thinking about him a lot lately.

285
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,120
Every time I see a tree,

286
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:15,360
I think of that little guy.

287
00:14:18,799 --> 00:14:21,440
Say, if he came to the city,

288
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:22,360
would he get used to it?

289
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,279
Seeing the trees here,

290
00:14:25,519 --> 00:14:26,480
would he adapt?

291
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:27,399
He's so young.

292
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:28,759
I don't know.

293
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:30,639
But the trees in the city

294
00:14:30,639 --> 00:14:31,919
are really different from the ones in the mountains.

295
00:14:32,759 --> 00:14:34,679
You see, mountain trees have their own personalities.

296
00:14:34,679 --> 00:14:35,840
And their own names.

297
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,480
But the trees in the city

298
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,759
are all trimmed so neatly.

299
00:14:39,159 --> 00:14:40,840
A soul as wild,

300
00:14:40,879 --> 00:14:41,960
as free,

301
00:14:42,039 --> 00:14:43,720
and as full of life as Yang A'wu...

302
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:47,759
He was born for that mountain forest.

303
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:52,000
You know what?

304
00:14:52,919 --> 00:14:53,919
He even showed me

305
00:14:53,919 --> 00:14:55,759
the graves they dug under the trees.

306
00:14:56,519 --> 00:14:57,480
What graves?

307
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:01,120
It means while they're still alive,

308
00:15:01,399 --> 00:15:02,240
they already dig a hole for themselves

309
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:04,279
to mark where they'll be buried after they die.

310
00:15:06,399 --> 00:15:07,240
That's pretty interesting.

311
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:09,840
It means he wants to

312
00:15:10,799 --> 00:15:12,960
leave his final nutrients

313
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:14,360
to the tree he loves the most.

314
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:17,320
Just like city folks

315
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,399
leaving their inheritance to the ones they love.

316
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:28,840
Then why don't you go see him,

317
00:15:29,159 --> 00:15:30,000
or contact him?

318
00:15:32,039 --> 00:15:33,720
I heard he's about to be

319
00:15:33,879 --> 00:15:35,480
taken to his adoptive parents' house.

320
00:15:36,639 --> 00:15:38,679
Do you have his adoptive parents' contact info?

321
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:41,559
Why would I have their contact info?

322
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:42,720
Fair enough.

323
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:46,360
But his adoptive parents must be good people, right?

324
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,200
Look at Lao Kang.

325
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:50,960
He tried so hard to stop them from taking the kid back before,

326
00:15:51,799 --> 00:15:52,960
but when Lao Kang got into trouble,

327
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:54,480
they were still willing to find someone to help him.

328
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,120
I hope so.

329
00:15:59,559 --> 00:16:00,840
I'd really love to meet him.

330
00:16:03,759 --> 00:16:05,000
Why are you so interested

331
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,000
in this little kid?

332
00:16:07,879 --> 00:16:09,679
Because my son,

333
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,840
when he was his age,

334
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,279
was the closest to me.

335
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:17,639
Kids around this age

336
00:16:17,639 --> 00:16:19,399
are like alarms.

337
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,799
Whenever they're unhappy, they yell.

338
00:16:21,799 --> 00:16:23,080
Like, they really scream.

339
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:25,159
Just...

340
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:27,279
about so many things.

341
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,279
Do you think it's genetic?

342
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:33,559
Inherited from whom?

343
00:16:34,480 --> 00:16:35,840
I was never like that.

344
00:16:37,759 --> 00:16:39,279
I kept everything bottled up inside.

345
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:44,759
This sweet soup is really good!

346
00:16:44,919 --> 00:16:45,480
Yeah?

347
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:47,039
No wonder the line was so long.

348
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,480
Waiting in line is pretty interesting.

349
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:52,279
You never know if you'll

350
00:16:52,279 --> 00:16:53,480
actually get your turn, you know?

351
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:55,320
You just keep waiting.

352
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:58,279
You worry that when it's finally your turn,

353
00:16:59,279 --> 00:17:00,600
it might be sold out. What then?

354
00:17:01,559 --> 00:17:02,600
You line up again tomorrow.

355
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:07,359
Who knows if we even have a tomorrow?

356
00:17:09,759 --> 00:17:10,920
Why so pessimistic?

357
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,880
No, what if tomorrow I forget

358
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:13,880
the address of the sweet soup shop?

359
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:14,519
What then?

360
00:17:14,519 --> 00:17:16,440
You know I have Alzheimer's,

361
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:17,720
right?

362
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:19,480
Then I'll be the one waiting in line to buy it for you.

363
00:18:11,319 --> 00:18:12,079
The kid ran away!

364
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:13,480
The kid ran away!

365
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,279
He might be over there.

366
00:18:14,279 --> 00:18:15,400
Let's go check.

367
00:18:39,319 --> 00:18:40,440
Hello, Mr. Yu.

368
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:41,359
Hello, Ding Ning.

369
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:43,480
What are you doing? I told you there's no rush.

370
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:47,119
Why did you transfer the money to me so fast?

371
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:49,839
I'm definitely not going to Rongshan.

372
00:18:49,839 --> 00:18:50,559
So...

373
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:54,559
Hang on a second.

374
00:18:58,119 --> 00:18:58,880
Hello?

375
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:00,200
Is this Lawyer Ding Ning?

376
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:02,640
Speaking.

377
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:04,799
Hello, this is the Nanfeng Road Police Station.

378
00:19:04,799 --> 00:19:06,680
Could you come to Limin Square on Nanfeng Road?

379
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,519
Okay, I'll head over right now.

380
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:10,720
Bye.

381
00:19:12,119 --> 00:19:14,160
Mr. Yu, something urgent came up.

382
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:15,440
I have to go to Nanfeng Road right now.

383
00:19:21,279 --> 00:19:22,279
Nanfeng Road?

384
00:19:23,480 --> 00:19:24,440
What for?

385
00:19:29,359 --> 00:19:30,880
Whose kid is this?

386
00:19:33,079 --> 00:19:35,400
Hurry up and come down. It's dangerous up there.

387
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:42,279
Look.

388
00:19:42,279 --> 00:19:44,240
There are too many people here at the scene right now.

389
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:45,160
We need to ensure safety.

390
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:46,039
And one more thing.

391
00:19:46,119 --> 00:19:46,759
We need to notify the fire department.

392
00:19:46,759 --> 00:19:47,839
Hello, I'm Ding Ning.

393
00:19:47,839 --> 00:19:49,640
Did you call me?

394
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:50,400
You're Ding Ning, right?

395
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:51,359
I'm the one who called you.

396
00:19:51,359 --> 00:19:52,440
Come here for a second.

397
00:19:53,759 --> 00:19:54,920
Do you know this kid?

398
00:19:56,079 --> 00:19:57,039
Yang A'wu?

399
00:19:57,519 --> 00:19:58,640
What are you doing here?

400
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:01,119
I know him. I know this boy.

401
00:20:01,319 --> 00:20:02,680
He hasn't said a word.

402
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:03,640
And we found you...

403
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:05,599
...from a business card that fell out of his pocket.

404
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:09,000
This kid usually lives in the mountains.

405
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,720
I guess he just arrived in the city.

406
00:20:11,079 --> 00:20:12,559
He probably panicked and got lost.

407
00:20:12,559 --> 00:20:13,359
And then he climbed up there.

408
00:20:13,359 --> 00:20:14,079
I'll call him down.

409
00:20:14,079 --> 00:20:14,599
Okay.

410
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:15,720
A'wu!

411
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:17,640
Ding Ning, Ding Ning.

412
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:19,240
Come on down.

413
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:21,039
Slowly, kid.

414
00:20:21,039 --> 00:20:21,960
We'll catch you.

415
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:22,480
Come on, get down.

416
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:23,200
Careful, careful.

417
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:26,200
Watch your step.

418
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:26,960
Hold on tight.

419
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:27,599
Be careful.

420
00:20:29,039 --> 00:20:30,119
Slowly, slowly.

421
00:20:30,119 --> 00:20:30,799
Easy now.

422
00:20:32,279 --> 00:20:32,920
Come here, I'll catch you.

423
00:20:42,799 --> 00:20:43,559
Careful.

424
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:45,920
Watch your step. No rush.

425
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:46,839
It's fine, he can do it.

426
00:20:47,319 --> 00:20:48,119
Come on, get down.

427
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:55,400
A'wu.

428
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:57,200
A'wu, how did you get here?

429
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:58,240
Who brought you here?

430
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:00,359
Who brought you here?

431
00:21:01,359 --> 00:21:04,440
This kid climbs trees whenever he gets scared.

432
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:05,680
That's quite unusual.

433
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:07,039
What's his name?

434
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:08,359
Yang A'wu.

435
00:21:08,359 --> 00:21:09,279
Yang as in poplar tree.

436
00:21:09,279 --> 00:21:10,240
And A'wu as in the number five.

437
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:11,960
Yang A'wu.

438
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:12,519
A'wu.

439
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:13,000
Go to the...

440
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:13,720
Come here, it's okay.

441
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:15,200
...missing persons database and look up this name.

442
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:16,039
I'm right here.

443
00:21:17,519 --> 00:21:18,640
How many days have you been here?

444
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:20,240
Your hair is such a mess.

445
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:21,359
Alright, everything's fine now.

446
00:21:21,359 --> 00:21:22,319
Break it up. Time to go home.

447
00:21:22,319 --> 00:21:23,359
How did you get here?

448
00:21:24,559 --> 00:21:25,759
Who brought you here?

449
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:49,200
Yang A'wu

450
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:54,680
Mr. Yu, why are you here?

451
00:22:03,039 --> 00:22:04,799
Sir, you are...?

452
00:22:05,279 --> 00:22:06,160
We know each other.

453
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:09,119
This is...

454
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:10,880
Please check Yang A'wu's registry info.

455
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:12,599
You know him?

456
00:22:13,039 --> 00:22:14,240
He's about 1.2 meters tall.

457
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:18,839
I know his adoptive father.

458
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:21,000
You know his adoptive father?

459
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:21,440
Yes.

460
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,319
What's his adoptive father's name?

461
00:22:22,759 --> 00:22:23,200
Just a second.

462
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:24,039
Zhao Yijie.

463
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:26,160
Transfer to Zhao Yijie.

464
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:27,759
Please put me through to Zhao Yijie.

465
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:29,799
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

466
00:22:29,799 --> 00:22:30,519
Hello, Mr. Zhao.

467
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:32,079
I'm an officer from the Nanfeng Road Police Station.

468
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:33,119
The child has been found.

469
00:22:33,119 --> 00:22:33,960
Where are you?

470
00:22:34,359 --> 00:22:34,720
I'm sorry.

471
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:35,680
I'm out of town right now.

472
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:39,200
Is your dad's name Zhao Yijie?

473
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:40,880
Then what about the child?

474
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:43,079
Can I speak with him?

475
00:22:46,119 --> 00:22:47,000
What's the situation?

476
00:22:47,119 --> 00:22:48,519
Hello? Zhao Yijie.

477
00:22:48,680 --> 00:22:49,559
Yu Songfan.

478
00:22:49,559 --> 00:22:50,480
Yu Songfan.

479
00:22:50,759 --> 00:22:51,799
Why are you there?

480
00:22:51,799 --> 00:22:54,519
I've already found the child for you.

481
00:22:54,839 --> 00:22:56,839
I'll take care of him for you tonight.

482
00:22:57,079 --> 00:22:58,079
Let him stay at my place.

483
00:22:58,079 --> 00:22:58,799
Don't even think about it.

484
00:22:58,799 --> 00:23:00,240
I'll have the nanny pick him up right now.

485
00:23:00,519 --> 00:23:02,440
Didn't the nanny already lose him?

486
00:23:02,599 --> 00:23:04,440
Do you want to lose him again?

487
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:05,920
Listen to me.

488
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:07,559
He's staying at my place tonight.

489
00:23:08,160 --> 00:23:09,680
Do you understand?

490
00:23:10,599 --> 00:23:11,839
That's settled then. You're welcome.

491
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:13,799
Then explain it to the police.

492
00:23:15,960 --> 00:23:16,759
Hello, Mr. Zhao.

493
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:18,680
Please leave the child with my friend for now.

494
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:19,319
Okay.

495
00:23:19,519 --> 00:23:20,920
You're lucky to have a good friend.

496
00:23:21,759 --> 00:23:23,240
All right, we'll leave the child with you.

497
00:23:24,759 --> 00:23:25,720
Thank you. Sorry for the trouble.

498
00:23:26,079 --> 00:23:26,599
No problem.

499
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:32,160
Let's go home.

500
00:23:53,240 --> 00:23:54,799
Come on in. No need to take off your shoes.

501
00:23:59,119 --> 00:24:00,160
Okay, okay. Let's go in.

502
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:01,599
Have a seat inside.

503
00:24:02,839 --> 00:24:04,160
Do you want some milk?

504
00:24:04,319 --> 00:24:05,400
How about some milk?

505
00:24:05,799 --> 00:24:06,599
Do you want some?

506
00:24:09,440 --> 00:24:10,599
So you're saying

507
00:24:11,359 --> 00:24:13,359
Yang A'wu's adoptive father is Zhao Yijie?

508
00:24:13,359 --> 00:24:14,559
It's because he used to

509
00:24:14,559 --> 00:24:16,400
frequently donate to schools in Rongshan.

510
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:18,599
That's how he met A'wu

511
00:24:18,799 --> 00:24:19,839
and adopted him.

512
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:21,119
Yeah.

513
00:24:21,279 --> 00:24:24,200
He showed me a photo of the three of them,

514
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:26,880
so I know what he looks like.

515
00:24:26,880 --> 00:24:28,720
But I didn't know his name.

516
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:32,920
That's really unexpected.

517
00:24:32,920 --> 00:24:36,079
Later, you kept mentioning Yang A'wu,

518
00:24:36,599 --> 00:24:37,880
turns out it's the same person.

519
00:24:37,880 --> 00:24:38,640
What a coincidence.

520
00:24:38,799 --> 00:24:39,799
A'wu, A'wu!

521
00:24:39,799 --> 00:24:40,720
Can you get down first?

522
00:24:40,720 --> 00:24:41,960
I can't breathe like this, A'wu!

523
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:42,839
A'wu!

524
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:51,440
The alarm. I see what you mean.

525
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:52,759
What should we do?

526
00:24:53,839 --> 00:24:54,640
A'wu.

527
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,799
A'wu, can you sit down for a bit?

528
00:24:56,880 --> 00:24:57,480
A'wu!

529
00:24:57,960 --> 00:24:58,960
How about some milk? Milk.

530
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:00,599
A'wu, get down and sit for a moment.

531
00:25:00,759 --> 00:25:01,799
Ask him to drink the milk.

532
00:25:01,799 --> 00:25:02,960
Look, look at this grandpa.

533
00:25:02,960 --> 00:25:03,920
Look at this grandpa.

534
00:25:03,920 --> 00:25:05,039
He's just like me.

535
00:25:05,039 --> 00:25:06,039
He's also your...

536
00:25:06,039 --> 00:25:07,440
Your Ga'ao, Ma Wei,

537
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:08,359
and Nezha.

538
00:25:08,680 --> 00:25:09,599
It's okay, don't be afraid.

539
00:25:09,599 --> 00:25:10,720
He's our friend.

540
00:25:10,799 --> 00:25:11,559
Don't be afraid.

541
00:25:11,640 --> 00:25:12,319
Look.

542
00:25:12,799 --> 00:25:14,039
What did you just say?

543
00:25:14,039 --> 00:25:14,839
Is that their hometown dialect?

544
00:25:14,839 --> 00:25:15,200
Come on.

545
00:25:15,359 --> 00:25:15,920
Do you want the milk?

546
00:25:15,920 --> 00:25:16,839
It's delicious. Come here.

547
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:18,480
No.

548
00:25:18,680 --> 00:25:19,319
What does that mean?

549
00:25:19,319 --> 00:25:20,240
I told you before.

550
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:22,160
They're names he gave to trees.

551
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:24,640
A'wu, did you just fart?

552
00:25:26,200 --> 00:25:27,319
It stinks.

553
00:25:28,319 --> 00:25:29,359
Seriously.

554
00:25:31,319 --> 00:25:32,160
Take your time.

555
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:35,599
Drink up. Slowly now.

556
00:25:41,119 --> 00:25:43,119
That law firm Zhao Yijie started,

557
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:45,000
is it called Rujie?

558
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:48,920
What's wrong?

559
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:53,400
Where's your bathroom?

560
00:25:54,839 --> 00:25:56,000
First door on the right.

561
00:25:57,200 --> 00:25:57,920
I need to use it.

562
00:25:58,119 --> 00:25:59,000
Sit here for a bit.

563
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:20,519
Hello, Zhou Hao.

564
00:26:22,319 --> 00:26:24,039
The case you asked me to join,

565
00:26:24,200 --> 00:26:26,440
