566
00:26:26,680 --> 00:26:27,599
How did you know?

567
00:26:31,559 --> 00:26:32,319
Forty-sixty split.

568
00:26:32,319 --> 00:26:32,960
Of course.

569
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:34,559
Then I'll send you the files right away.

570
00:26:35,039 --> 00:26:35,599
Okay.

571
00:26:52,720 --> 00:26:53,599
He fell asleep.

572
00:26:54,160 --> 00:26:57,079
He must have been through a lot lately.

573
00:26:57,079 --> 00:26:57,960
Didn't get much sleep.

574
00:26:59,599 --> 00:27:00,240
Let's have something to eat.

575
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:01,000
What would you like?

576
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Any dietary restrictions?

577
00:27:02,119 --> 00:27:02,880
No need to bother.

578
00:27:02,880 --> 00:27:03,920
I should probably head back.

579
00:27:05,640 --> 00:27:06,200
Ding Ning.

580
00:27:06,200 --> 00:27:08,000
I actually have a favor to ask.

581
00:27:09,680 --> 00:27:11,440
Could you stay here tonight?

582
00:27:12,599 --> 00:27:15,279
Because I'm worried that when the little guy wakes up...

583
00:27:15,279 --> 00:27:16,559
...his alarm will go off again.

584
00:27:16,559 --> 00:27:17,480
And I won't be able to handle him.

585
00:27:17,640 --> 00:27:19,000
What if he runs off again?

586
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:20,960
It'd be really hard to explain to his parents.

587
00:27:21,079 --> 00:27:21,799
Just for one night.

588
00:27:21,799 --> 00:27:23,039
Consider it doing me a favor, alright?

589
00:27:23,839 --> 00:27:24,480
I mean it.

590
00:27:25,519 --> 00:27:26,400
Stay at your place?

591
00:27:27,400 --> 00:27:29,119
I have a spare room.

592
00:27:31,119 --> 00:27:33,720
No, that wouldn't be appropriate.

593
00:27:34,759 --> 00:27:35,640
How about this?

594
00:27:36,160 --> 00:27:37,960
If he wakes up and makes a fuss again...

595
00:27:38,079 --> 00:27:39,160
...just give me a call.

596
00:27:39,160 --> 00:27:39,880
As long as I'm not busy...

597
00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:41,680
...I'll come right over to help look after him, okay?

598
00:27:41,720 --> 00:27:42,680
Call me, okay?

599
00:27:42,680 --> 00:27:43,799
Alright, sorry about this.

600
00:27:44,839 --> 00:27:45,400
I'm leaving now.

601
00:27:53,519 --> 00:27:54,000
A'wu.

602
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:54,960
I have to go back.

603
00:27:54,960 --> 00:27:56,799
Ding Ning is leaving. Come here.

604
00:27:58,880 --> 00:27:59,640
See?

605
00:28:03,240 --> 00:28:04,359
A'wu, I have to go back.

606
00:28:04,359 --> 00:28:05,319
I don't live here.

607
00:28:05,319 --> 00:28:07,160
You stay here with Grandpa, okay?

608
00:28:07,160 --> 00:28:08,000
Hear me? Come here.

609
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:11,359
How about you stay for dinner?

610
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:12,359
What do you want to eat?

611
00:28:12,440 --> 00:28:13,119
I don't have any dietary restrictions.

612
00:28:13,119 --> 00:28:14,240
I'll go start cooking.

613
00:28:14,680 --> 00:28:15,440
No, I...

614
00:28:16,400 --> 00:28:17,119
It's okay.

615
00:28:19,559 --> 00:28:20,200
A'wu.

616
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:24,799
A'wu.

617
00:28:26,480 --> 00:28:28,119
Can you get down for a second?

618
00:28:28,519 --> 00:28:29,279
A'wu.

619
00:28:29,640 --> 00:28:30,759
A'wu, okay.

620
00:28:30,759 --> 00:28:32,680
I... I came back, didn't I?

621
00:28:33,799 --> 00:28:35,640
How about tomato and tomato stir-fry?

622
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:41,480
I mean eggs.

623
00:28:57,319 --> 00:28:58,039
Alright.

624
00:28:58,960 --> 00:29:00,960
I'm heading to Rongshan again in a few days anyway.

625
00:29:01,359 --> 00:29:03,240
Didn't you turn down Lao Kang's case?

626
00:29:03,240 --> 00:29:04,559
Why are you going to Rongshan?

627
00:29:04,680 --> 00:29:05,480
I didn't.

628
00:29:05,519 --> 00:29:06,160
Right now, I'm

629
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:08,000
the assistant lawyer for Lao Kang's case.

630
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:10,759
They said this case involves a jurisdictional challenge,

631
00:29:11,200 --> 00:29:12,119
so it's highly likely

632
00:29:12,119 --> 00:29:13,880
it'll be sent back to the county court for trial.

633
00:29:13,880 --> 00:29:15,440
A'wu. A'wu.

634
00:29:15,519 --> 00:29:16,720
Jurisdictional challenge.

635
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:19,319
A'wu, Grandpa made you something delicious.

636
00:29:19,519 --> 00:29:20,599
Do you like eggs?

637
00:29:20,799 --> 00:29:21,720
Or do you prefer meat?

638
00:29:21,720 --> 00:29:23,279
Look, see, Grandpa is cooking.

639
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:24,119
Time to eat!

640
00:29:24,119 --> 00:29:25,000
Are you getting hungry?

641
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:25,920
What's your favorite food?

642
00:29:26,799 --> 00:29:28,599
Do you like tomatoes stir-fried with tomatoes?

643
00:29:28,799 --> 00:29:30,839
My favorite thing to eat

644
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:32,119
is you!

645
00:29:35,079 --> 00:29:36,279
Are you ticklish?

646
00:29:36,559 --> 00:29:37,640
So ticklish!

647
00:30:30,279 --> 00:30:31,319
In Lao Kang's case,

648
00:30:31,519 --> 00:30:33,160
Zhou Hao raised a jurisdictional challenge.

649
00:30:54,440 --> 00:30:55,240
Mr. Zhao.

650
00:30:55,400 --> 00:30:57,079
What's going on with the jurisdictional challenge?

651
00:30:57,160 --> 00:30:59,519
I was just making a presentation to report to you.

652
00:30:59,640 --> 00:31:01,839
Should I just give you a verbal update now?

653
00:31:01,839 --> 00:31:02,440
Go ahead.

654
00:31:02,799 --> 00:31:05,319
I think this case of ours is very strange.

655
00:31:05,559 --> 00:31:07,279
It's moving incredibly fast.

656
00:31:07,480 --> 00:31:09,440
I haven't even had time to meet with Lao Kang,

657
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:11,279
and the investigation phase is already over.

658
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:13,559
It's moving to the procuratorate's review for prosecution.

659
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:14,839
So?

660
00:31:14,960 --> 00:31:16,359
Just hear me out.

661
00:31:16,960 --> 00:31:18,160
For Lao Kang's case,

662
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:20,160
I have my own strategy.

663
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:22,799
There's a young judge at Fulin District Court

664
00:31:22,799 --> 00:31:24,720
who just transferred from Civil to Criminal.

665
00:31:24,799 --> 00:31:25,880
He told me that...

666
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:26,799
Listen to me carefully.

667
00:31:29,279 --> 00:31:31,640
Stop messing with the jurisdictional challenge.

668
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:33,720
The trial stays in the local court.

669
00:31:35,039 --> 00:31:35,799
Understood.

670
00:31:37,079 --> 00:31:40,880
I... I was just afraid there might be flaws in our case,

671
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:41,640
so I thought...

672
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:42,519
All right, that's enough.

673
00:31:42,799 --> 00:31:43,480
Thanks for your hard work.

674
00:31:50,960 --> 00:31:51,680
Just doing my job.

675
00:32:00,480 --> 00:32:01,200
Hey, Dad.

676
00:32:03,440 --> 00:32:04,759
It's pretty good.

677
00:32:05,839 --> 00:32:06,559
Going smoothly.

678
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:11,000
Rujie is better than I expected.

679
00:32:11,839 --> 00:32:13,160
I've taken on quite a few cases.

680
00:32:15,680 --> 00:32:16,960
Don't look down on me.

681
00:32:17,079 --> 00:32:18,039
I'm telling you,

682
00:32:18,240 --> 00:32:19,359
in another couple of years,

683
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:22,599
it'll be my turn to teach you about the law.

684
00:32:22,759 --> 00:32:23,759
You hear me?

685
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:27,799
Make sure you take your medicine on time.

686
00:32:30,319 --> 00:32:31,119
Morning.

687
00:32:32,599 --> 00:32:33,640
Did you sleep okay last night?

688
00:32:34,599 --> 00:32:35,319
Not bad.

689
00:32:35,720 --> 00:32:37,759
I'm sorry to trouble you.

690
00:32:37,839 --> 00:32:38,559
Um,

691
00:32:39,160 --> 00:32:41,319
when is lawyer Zhao Yijie coming to pick him up?

692
00:32:41,759 --> 00:32:44,160
I called him last night.

693
00:32:44,200 --> 00:32:46,000
He said he had to go on a business trip.

694
00:32:46,680 --> 00:32:47,759
I'm so annoyed.

695
00:32:47,759 --> 00:32:50,400
He said he won't be back for a while.

696
00:32:50,720 --> 00:32:51,519
I really...

697
00:32:51,720 --> 00:32:53,440
I really don't know what to do now.

698
00:32:56,880 --> 00:32:58,359
I just feel that

699
00:32:58,880 --> 00:33:00,839
my staying here like this isn't a solution.

700
00:33:00,839 --> 00:33:02,200
And I haven't checked out of the hotel yet.

701
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:03,400
I know.

702
00:33:03,680 --> 00:33:04,720
I just feel bad about it.

703
00:33:04,720 --> 00:33:06,240
I really don't know what to say.

704
00:33:06,440 --> 00:33:07,880
Really, sorry to bother you.

705
00:33:17,319 --> 00:33:18,079
A'wu.

706
00:33:18,599 --> 00:33:19,319
A'wu.

707
00:33:19,640 --> 00:33:21,359
Here, here, here.

708
00:33:24,160 --> 00:33:24,920
A'wu.

709
00:33:26,920 --> 00:33:29,200
Why are you hiding under the table to eat?

710
00:33:30,880 --> 00:33:31,240
Come on out.

711
00:33:31,240 --> 00:33:32,319
It's too dusty down here, okay?

712
00:33:32,319 --> 00:33:33,319
Come out and eat, alright?

713
00:33:33,319 --> 00:33:33,839
Come on out.

714
00:33:33,839 --> 00:33:34,920
Come on, come out.

715
00:33:35,039 --> 00:33:35,839
Eat.

716
00:33:36,160 --> 00:33:37,400
It's dusty down here.

717
00:33:37,799 --> 00:33:39,640
What if you get sick?

718
00:33:39,640 --> 00:33:40,640
Come out, be a good boy.

719
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:41,440
Oh, A'wu...

720
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:43,680
A'wu, do you want to eat down here?

721
00:33:44,880 --> 00:33:45,599
Okay.

722
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:47,240
A'wu.

723
00:33:47,720 --> 00:33:48,880
Come on, we'll eat down here.

724
00:33:48,880 --> 00:33:50,200
I'll eat down here with you, okay?

725
00:33:50,200 --> 00:33:51,799
Ding Ning, you shouldn't do that.

726
00:33:51,799 --> 00:33:53,160
There are rules for eating.

727
00:33:53,160 --> 00:33:54,880
You should eat at the table.

728
00:33:55,599 --> 00:33:56,480
Just take it slow.

729
00:33:56,480 --> 00:33:58,519
You have to give him time to adapt.

730
00:34:00,359 --> 00:34:01,359
Alright then. Okay, okay.

731
00:34:01,359 --> 00:34:02,319
You're giving this to me?

732
00:34:02,400 --> 00:34:03,200
Okay, okay, okay.

733
00:34:03,200 --> 00:34:04,720
We'll stay right here together.

734
00:34:04,720 --> 00:34:05,960
And eat down here, okay?

735
00:34:05,960 --> 00:34:06,839
It's so tasty!

736
00:34:06,839 --> 00:34:08,079
We'll all eat down here.

737
00:34:08,360 --> 00:34:10,079
I'll eat down here too, alright?

738
00:34:10,079 --> 00:34:11,599
Let's all eat down here together, okay?

739
00:34:13,039 --> 00:34:13,960
It's very tasty.

740
00:34:14,079 --> 00:34:16,039
It's like being under a big tree, isn't it?

741
00:34:16,920 --> 00:34:17,679
Is it good?

742
00:34:18,239 --> 00:34:19,039
It's good, right?

743
00:34:19,280 --> 00:34:20,760
Grandpa made all of this.

744
00:34:20,960 --> 00:34:21,719
Yeah.

745
00:34:22,039 --> 00:34:24,280
From now on, Grandpa will cook good food for you.

746
00:34:24,280 --> 00:34:25,039
Okay?

747
00:34:25,039 --> 00:34:25,639
Is it tasty?

748
00:34:25,639 --> 00:34:26,760
Is Grandpa's cooking good?

749
00:34:26,760 --> 00:34:29,039
Tasty, tasty.

750
00:34:29,119 --> 00:34:31,320
A'wu says it's tasty.

751
00:34:31,599 --> 00:34:33,679
Tasty.

752
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:34,639
That's right.

753
00:34:34,639 --> 00:34:35,679
Great job.

754
00:34:35,679 --> 00:34:36,440
So tasty.

755
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:38,280
Eat some more.

756
00:34:38,280 --> 00:34:39,079
Grandpa.

757
00:34:40,159 --> 00:34:40,800
Grandpa.

758
00:34:41,599 --> 00:34:43,599
I'm Grandpa.

759
00:34:44,199 --> 00:34:46,039
Grandpa.

760
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:49,760
Grandpa. Grandpa.

761
00:34:52,519 --> 00:34:53,760
A'wu just called me Grandpa.

762
00:34:54,079 --> 00:34:56,039
Say it again. Grandpa.

763
00:34:56,039 --> 00:34:56,800
Eat up.

764
00:34:57,159 --> 00:34:58,239
Say it one more time, okay?

765
00:34:59,599 --> 00:35:01,599
Grandpa.

766
00:35:07,559 --> 00:35:08,840
He learns so fast.

767
00:35:09,480 --> 00:35:10,360
He learns very fast.

768
00:35:34,679 --> 00:35:37,119
A'wu, I have to go to work today.

769
00:35:38,119 --> 00:35:40,159
You stay home and play with Grandpa, okay?

770
00:35:40,920 --> 00:35:42,079
I'll be back soon.

771
00:35:42,079 --> 00:35:42,880
I'll come back right after work, okay?

772
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:43,519
Morning, Mr. Yu.

773
00:35:44,079 --> 00:35:44,719
Hello.

774
00:35:49,920 --> 00:35:50,599
Alright.

775
00:35:50,960 --> 00:35:51,800
Be good.

776
00:35:52,599 --> 00:35:53,599
Stay with Grandpa.

777
00:35:53,840 --> 00:35:54,480
I'm heading out.

778
00:36:11,679 --> 00:36:12,800
Do you have the transcript?

779
00:36:13,719 --> 00:36:14,440
The transcript?

780
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:55,679
Pulled an all-nighter.

781
00:36:56,199 --> 00:36:57,400
Notice any changes?

782
00:36:59,960 --> 00:37:00,800
You look haggard.

783
00:37:01,840 --> 00:37:03,719
Dark circles, crow's feet.

784
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:07,719
And a bit of stubble.

785
00:37:08,639 --> 00:37:09,880
Do I look more mature?

786
00:37:12,400 --> 00:37:14,440
Since when is being clean-cut a burden?

787
00:37:15,039 --> 00:37:15,800
What?

788
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:16,800
Dark circles and crow's feet...

789
00:37:16,800 --> 00:37:18,159
Can they help you win cases?

790
00:37:18,159 --> 00:37:19,679
Of course.

791
00:37:20,719 --> 00:37:22,960
They make my clients trust me more.

792
00:37:23,440 --> 00:37:24,239
And I can take this...

793
00:37:24,239 --> 00:37:25,559
Let me remind you.

794
00:37:25,960 --> 00:37:26,840
If we go back now,

795
00:37:26,840 --> 00:37:28,719
we can freshen up and still get two hours of sleep

796
00:37:28,719 --> 00:37:30,000
before seeing Lao Kang.

797
00:37:38,119 --> 00:37:39,159
You don't need a ride?

798
00:37:40,119 --> 00:37:40,880
I'll take a cab.

799
00:37:50,519 --> 00:37:51,239
Morning.

800
00:37:51,480 --> 00:37:53,000
Judge Yu, long time no see.

801
00:37:53,360 --> 00:37:54,119
Wontons, please.

802
00:37:54,119 --> 00:37:55,039
Coming right up!

803
00:37:55,039 --> 00:37:56,519
Haven't had your wontons in a while.

804
00:37:56,519 --> 00:37:57,360
Mr. Yu.

805
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:00,000
Mr. Yu.

806
00:38:00,960 --> 00:38:02,360
It's me, Sun from the Civil Division.

807
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:05,199
Hello, hello, Sun.

808
00:38:05,199 --> 00:38:06,880
Why did you ignore me just now?

809
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:07,960
I didn't, it's just...

810
00:38:08,599 --> 00:38:10,519
because of how I've been lately,

811
00:38:10,519 --> 00:38:11,880
I didn't dare to hang around you guys.

812
00:38:11,880 --> 00:38:13,440
I didn't want to bring you young folks down.

813
00:38:13,960 --> 00:38:15,760
Don't say that, Mr. Yu.

814
00:38:16,199 --> 00:38:17,280
After what happened to you,

815
00:38:17,280 --> 00:38:18,840
I really wanted to visit you at home.

816
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:19,679
But you know,

817
00:38:19,679 --> 00:38:21,760
we rarely get to interact privately.

818
00:38:21,760 --> 00:38:23,440
I couldn't find your place and was worried.

819
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:24,760
What's the matter, Sun?

820
00:38:24,760 --> 00:38:25,679
How have you been lately?

821
00:38:26,840 --> 00:38:27,920
I transferred to the Criminal Division.

822
00:38:28,760 --> 00:38:29,519
That's great!

823
00:38:30,199 --> 00:38:33,239
You've always wanted to move from Civil to Criminal.

824
00:38:33,599 --> 00:38:35,760
Your wish finally came true. Congratulations!

825
00:38:35,760 --> 00:38:36,760
Not really, Mr. Yu.

826
00:38:36,760 --> 00:38:37,880
After I transferred there,

827
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:39,639
I finally remembered what you told me before.

828
00:38:39,960 --> 00:38:41,039
"It's the same everywhere."

829
00:38:41,039 --> 00:38:43,679
I used to hate the busywork in Civil.

830
00:38:43,679 --> 00:38:44,400
And now look at me.

831
00:38:44,400 --> 00:38:45,719
I work overtime every day in Criminal.

832
00:38:45,719 --> 00:38:46,480
It's so annoying.

833
00:38:46,880 --> 00:38:47,960
You'll get used to it eventually.

834
00:38:57,400 --> 00:38:58,159
Mr. Yu.

835
00:38:58,400 --> 00:38:59,840
Glad I ran into you today.

836
00:39:00,039 --> 00:39:01,519
Could you give me some pointers?

837
00:39:02,119 --> 00:39:03,880
If I want my skills in the criminal division

838
00:39:03,880 --> 00:39:06,239
to improve quickly in all aspects,

839
00:39:06,639 --> 00:39:08,760
what exactly should I focus on?

840
00:39:09,559 --> 00:39:13,119
Sun, I really shouldn't spout nonsense.

841
00:39:13,440 --> 00:39:14,360
How could it be nonsense?

842
00:39:14,360 --> 00:39:15,960
You're a leading expert, Mr. Yu.

843
00:39:18,639 --> 00:39:20,920
Is it fraud cases?

844
00:39:21,920 --> 00:39:23,039
What I mean is,

845
00:39:23,039 --> 00:39:25,199
I need to have my own area of expertise

846
00:39:25,199 --> 00:39:27,360
to avoid low-end competition.

847
00:39:27,360 --> 00:39:28,760
Something with good prospects.

848
00:39:28,920 --> 00:39:31,719
To be honest, Sun, if you really want my advice,

849
00:39:32,039 --> 00:39:34,840
it's best not to be too ambitious too soon.

850
00:39:35,440 --> 00:39:36,360
If you're thinking like this,

851
00:39:36,360 --> 00:39:38,320
others are thinking the same way.

852
00:39:38,519 --> 00:39:41,000
Everyone wants to stand out.

853
00:39:41,559 --> 00:39:43,559
Everyone wants to take shortcuts.

854
00:39:44,079 --> 00:39:45,440
So in the court,

855
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:47,480
people who can do solid, steady work

856
00:39:47,480 --> 00:39:50,559
are extremely rare.

857
00:39:51,480 --> 00:39:52,159
Actually,

858
00:39:52,159 --> 00:39:54,480
the easiest way to stand out in Criminal...

859
00:39:54,480 --> 00:39:55,559
W-What is it?

860
00:39:56,960 --> 00:39:59,000
is being a steady judge.

861
00:39:59,800 --> 00:40:01,079
You're new here,

862
00:40:01,119 --> 00:40:02,800
so it's best not to be overly ambitious

863
00:40:02,800 --> 00:40:04,800
and rush to take on major cases.

864
00:40:04,800 --> 00:40:06,840
You need to know how to pick case types.

865
00:40:07,239 --> 00:40:10,840
Some minor cases within major anti-gang operations,

866
00:40:11,079 --> 00:40:12,559
the most inconspicuous ones,

867
00:40:12,599 --> 00:40:14,159
for example, illegal possession

868
00:40:14,639 --> 00:40:15,800
or picking quarrels and provoking trouble.

869
00:40:16,199 --> 00:40:17,079
Right.

870
00:40:17,079 --> 00:40:18,119
Cases like those.

871
00:40:18,119 --> 00:40:19,519
Because for these minor cases,

872
00:40:19,519 --> 00:40:20,280
you can refer to

873
00:40:20,280 --> 00:40:22,639
how other judges and courts rule.

874
00:40:22,800 --> 00:40:25,159
You should also frequently sit down with seniors

875
00:40:25,159 --> 00:40:28,039
to hold meetings and study them together.

876
00:40:28,639 --> 00:40:30,159
Discussing things like this

877
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:32,320
is also an opportunity to be noticed.

878
00:40:32,800 --> 00:40:34,440
You really are something, Mr. Yu.

879
00:40:36,840 --> 00:40:40,800
For cases involving jurisdictional challenges,

880
00:40:42,519 --> 00:40:44,639
you should dismiss them when appropriate.

881
00:40:45,320 --> 00:40:46,360
Don't push cases away,

882
00:40:46,679 --> 00:40:48,119
because it looks bad if word gets out.

883
00:40:48,280 --> 00:40:49,559
People won't say

884
00:40:50,079 --> 00:40:52,320
that the court has a backlog of cases

885
00:40:52,320 --> 00:40:54,280
causing an unreasonable workload.

886
00:40:54,280 --> 00:40:56,920
They won't say the judges are exhausted.

887
00:40:57,519 --> 00:40:59,559
They'll just say there's a problem with the judge,

888
00:41:00,639 --> 00:41:02,320
blindly pursuing a high clearance rate

889
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:04,079
and making the numbers look good.

890
00:41:04,639 --> 00:41:06,079
They'll only think

891
00:41:06,880 --> 00:41:07,880
that these young judges

892
00:41:07,880 --> 00:41:11,079
aren't proactive in their work.

893
00:41:12,320 --> 00:41:13,239
Older judges, on the other hand,

894
00:41:13,239 --> 00:41:16,119
aren't afraid of being talked about like that

895
00:41:16,320 --> 00:41:18,880
because they have experience and confidence.

896
00:41:19,000 --> 00:41:20,239
But you young people

897
00:41:20,239 --> 00:41:22,519
have to consider this, right?

898
00:41:22,679 --> 00:41:24,519
Right, they are seniors after all.

899
00:41:24,519 --> 00:41:24,880
Right?

900
00:41:25,679 --> 00:41:26,559
You really are something, Mr. Yu.

901
00:41:26,559 --> 00:41:27,559
You've thought it through so thoroughly.

902
00:41:27,559 --> 00:41:29,039
Sun, look at the time.

903
00:41:29,039 --> 00:41:29,760
Don't be late.

904
00:41:30,639 --> 00:41:31,719
You're right, Mr. Yu.

905
00:41:31,719 --> 00:41:32,480
Then some other time,

906
00:41:32,559 --> 00:41:33,440
I'll definitely pay you a visit, Mr. Yu.

907
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:34,079
Have a good day at work.

908
00:41:34,079 --> 00:41:34,960
Enjoy your meal, Mr. Yu.
